      "decision": "accept",
      "note": "Insertion verified at ar offset 199 of merged row m4cfac1c5. Reading the base rows directly: r00030 ends «…إِّلا لَدَیْکَ، وَ مَعَاکِفُ» and r00031 begins «الْهِمَمِ قَدْ تَعَطَّلَتْ…». The base rows split the single word pair «مَعَاکِفُ الْهِمَمِ» («the haltings of aspirations») with no separating whitespace, so an exact join renders «مَعَاکِفُالْهِمَمِ» — a non-word. One U+0020 restores the reading the source plainly intends. The surrounding Arabic is undivided: no character before or after is changed, and the two base rows are otherwise contiguous. This is a proposed editorial space, not a source character; I accept it as the minimum correction that makes the merged row readable. No other spacing proposal exists in this record."
